## Building a Plugin Framework

### The Plugin Interface

```xiom
interface Plugin {
  fn name(&self) -> Str;
  fn execute(&self, input: Str) -> Str;
}
```

### Plugin Implementations

```xiom
type UpperCasePlugin {}
fn UpperCasePlugin.name(&self) -> Str { "Uppercase" }
fn UpperCasePlugin.execute(&self, input: Str) -> Str { input.clone() }

type ReversePlugin {}
fn ReversePlugin.name(&self) -> Str { "Reverse" }
fn ReversePlugin.execute(&self, input: Str) -> Str {
  let mut result = "";
  let mut i = input.len();
  while i > 0 { i -= 1; result = string.str_concat(result, string.from_char(input.get(i).unwrap())); };
  result
}

type WordCountPlugin {}
fn WordCountPlugin.name(&self) -> Str { "Word Counter" }
fn WordCountPlugin.execute(&self, input: Str) -> Int { ... }
```

